  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life Saving Emergency Health Response through supporting gap in Primary Health Services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project is considered as a second phase of Supporting primary Health &amp; Nutrition interventions in NW Syria through three PHCs AlThawra PHC (Idleb) , Altuwama PHC (Aleppo) and Sosyan PHC (Aleppo) and the main focus of interventions will focus on NCDs and mental health activities beside the regular activities of RH, Nutrition, and enhancing the health infrastructure conditions by a rehabilitation works in Altuwama PHC. By the end of the project, the services will be delivered to 24636 direct beneficiaries divided into (3922 men, 9387 women, 5696 boys, 5631 girls).</narrative>
  </description>
